# Production environment for GitHub Pages frontend build.
#
# This file is NOT committed with secrets. It documents the variable
# that must be set as a GitHub Actions secret before the production
# build will work correctly.
#
# HOW TO SET UP:
#   1. Deploy the Django backend to Render (see backend/build.sh).
#   2. Copy the Render service URL, e.g. https://your-app.onrender.com
#   3. Go to your GitHub repo:
#      Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret
#   4. Name:  VITE_API_BASE_URL
#      Value: https://your-app.onrender.com/api
#
# The GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) already
# injects this secret as VITE_API_BASE_URL during the Vite build, so
# no source files need to be changed.
#
# For local development, VITE_API_BASE_URL is not set here intentionally.
# The frontend/src/services/api.js fallback (http://127.0.0.1:8000/api)
# will be used automatically when running `npm run dev` locally.
